          "summary": "Scaling robotic foundation models requires diverse training data and reliable evaluation environments.\nSimulation offers a scalable solution, yet existing generation pipelines remain constrained by predefined assets and skills, a disconnect between scene generation and task generation, and limited support for complex embodiments and physics. 模拟提供了一个可扩展的解决方案，但现有的生成管道仍然受到预定义的资源和技能的限制，场景生成和任务生成之间的脱节，以及对复杂实施例和物理的有限支持。\nWe introduce EmbodiedSmith, a framework for scalable embodied data generation through recursive self-improvement (RSI).\nEmbodiedSmith unifies asset, scene, and task generation in a pipeline that supports autonomous creation and language-driven customization. EmbodiedSmith将资产、场景和任务生成统一到一个支持自主创建和语言驱动的自定义的管道中。\nIts core is an agentic refinement loop: scene generation anticipates downstream task requirements, while task generation guides targeted scene edits, allowing scenes and tasks to iteratively improve one another. 其核心是一个代理细化循环：场景生成预测下游任务需求，而任务生成引导有针对性的场景编辑，允许场景和任务相互迭代改进。\nThis joint refinement improves task generation success, including for long-horizon tasks. 这种联合改进提高了任务生成成功率，包括长期任务。\nThe framework further supports mobile manipulators, humanoids, and dexterous hands, as well as interactions involving deformable objects and fluids, broadening the range of behaviors and physical phenomena represented in generated data. 该框架进一步支持移动机械手、人形机械手和灵巧的手，以及涉及可变形物体和流体的相互作用，拓宽了生成数据中表示的行为和物理现象的范围。\nTogether, these capabilities provide a flexible simulation engine for both robot pretraining and evaluation. 这些功能共同为机器人预训练和评估提供了灵活的模拟引擎。\nExtensive experiments validate the quality, diversity, and generation efficiency of the resulting data, while downstream policy experiments demonstrate that increased data diversity improves generalization. 广泛的实验验证了结果数据的质量、多样性和生成效率，而下游策略实验表明，增加数据多样性可提高泛化。",
