          "summary": "ReAct-based agents typically rely on a single LLM policy to propose actions, interact with the environment, and decide when a task is complete. 基于ReAct的代理通常依靠单个LLM策略来建议操作、与环境交互并决定任务何时完成。\nThis coupling makes action authorization and completion control difficult to enforce independently, allowing errors to propagate and unsupported completion claims to terminate execution. 这种耦合使得操作授权和完成控制难以独立实施，从而允许错误传播和不受支持的完成声明终止执行。\nWe introduce DeReAct, a modular agent architecture that externalizes two gating policies: a Critic that validates proposed actions before execution, and a Context Manager that reconstructs an environment-supported \\textsc{State} and certifies task completion. 我们引入了DeReAct ，这是一种模块化代理架构，它将两个门控策略外化：在执行之前验证建议操作的Critic ，以及重构环境支持的\\ textsc {State}并证明任务完成的Context Manager。\nAcross GAIA and SWE-bench Verified, DeReAct improves Pass@1 most for weaker Brain models, with gains of 6.5--7.0 points for Qwen3-Coder-480B and 4.2--5.2 points for Claude Sonnet~4.5; gains diminish as Brain capability increases. 在GAIA和SWE-bench Verified中， DeReAct对较弱Brain模型的Pass @ 1提升幅度最大， Qwen3-Coder-480B提升6.5--7.0分， Claude Sonnet ~4.5提升4.2--5.2分；随着Brain能力的提升，提升幅度减小。\nTrajectory and ablation analyses show that external gating is effective when targeted failures are sufficiently prevalent and the gating policy is itself sufficient. 轨迹和消融分析表明，当目标故障足够普遍且门控策略本身就足够时，外部门控是有效的。\nWith Claude Opus~4.5, Pass@1 remains comparable to ReAct, while DeReAct produces more evidence-complete and constraint-satisfying trajectories, indicating that completion control can trade earlier termination for stronger grounding. 在Claude Opus~4.5中， Pass @ 1仍然可以与ReAct相媲美，而DeReAct产生了更多的证据完整和约束满足的轨迹，这表明完成控制可以用更早的终止来换取更强的接地。\nOverall, DeReAct improves weaker agents while retaining grounding benefits as models strengthen. 总体而言，随着模型的加强， DeReAct可以改善较弱的代理，同时保留接地优势。",
