          "summary": "Security benchmarks for LLM-based agents often report the attack success rate (ASR) as a measure of model robustness and use these scores to compare different models and defense mechanisms, assuming that they describe the security of the agent. 基于LLM的代理的安全基准通常将攻击成功率（ ASR ）报告为模型鲁棒性的度量，并使用这些分数来比较不同的模型和防御机制，假设它们描述了代理的安全性。\nIn this paper, we explore whether it also influences the benchmark's measurement. 在本文中，我们将探讨它是否也会影响基准的测量。\nTo measure the effect of the benchmark representation, we introduce threat-preserving representation sensitivity (TPRS), which measures how much the ASR changes when we change the agent-visible representation while holding the underlying task, harmful action, security policy, ground truth, environment, and the evaluation criteria fixed. 为了衡量基准表示的效果，我们引入了威胁保留表示敏感性（ TPRS ） ，它衡量当我们更改代理可见表示时ASR的变化程度，同时保持基础任务、有害行为、安全策略、地面真相、环境和评估标准固定。\nOn Agent Security Bench (ASB), replacing threat-related tool names with threat-neutral names raises the committed attack success rate by 11.67 percentage points on GPT-5-mini and by 13.21 points on Claude Haiku 4.5. 在Agent Security Bench （ ASB ）上，将威胁相关工具名称替换为威胁中立名称，可使GPT-5-mini的承诺攻击成功率提高11.67个百分点， Claude Haiku 4.5提高13.21个百分点。\nOn MCPTox, replacing the original neutral tool name with an explicit threat-related name lowers the ASR by 11.00 percentage points on GPT-5-mini and 4.11 points on Claude Haiku 4.5. 在MCPTox上，用明确的威胁相关名称替换原始中立工具名称，可使GPT-5-mini的ASR降低11.00个百分点，使Claude Haiku 4.5的ASR降低4.11个百分点。\nOn AgentDojo, adding threat-related wording to the attack-relevant tool changes ASR by only 0.50 percentage points on GPT-4o-mini, yet the benign utility falls by 5.36 points on tasks requiring that tool. 在AgentDojo上，在攻击相关工具中添加与威胁相关的措辞只会使GPT-4o-mini的ASR降低0.50个百分点，而在需要该工具的任务上，该良性效用降低了5.36个百分点。\nWe ran an experiment on MCPTox where we observed that a threat-neutral name matched on token count, length, and casing reproduces most of the shift produced by the threat-explicit name (8.54 of 11.00 points on GPT-5-mini). 我们在MCPTox上进行了一项实验，观察到在令牌计数、长度和大小写上匹配的威胁中立名称重现了威胁明确名称产生的大部分转变（ GPT-5-mini上的11.00分中的8.54分）。\nThe results show that a security score measured under one representation may fail to generalize across threat-preserving representations of the same security problem. 结果表明，在一个表示法下测量的安全分数可能无法泛化相同安全问题的威胁保留表示法。\nRobustness claims should therefore be supported by performance across a controlled set of threat-preserving representations rather than relying on a single representation-dependent score. 因此，稳健性声明应该由一组受控的威胁保留表示的表现来支持，而不是依赖于单一的表示相关分数。",
