          "summary": "The rapid advancement of AI-generated video poses challenges to digital authenticity and security. 人工智能生成的视频的快速发展对数字真实性和安全性构成了挑战。\nCurrent detection methods, often trained on specific datasets, struggle with the ever-evolving landscape of generative techniques and unseen manipulations. 当前的检测方法通常在特定数据集上进行培训，难以应对不断发展的生成技术和看不见的操作。\nWe introduce a framework leveraging Vision Language Models (VLMs) for robust AI-generated video detection. 我们引入了一个利用视觉语言模型（ VLM ）的框架，用于强大的人工智能生成的视频检测。\nOur approach equips the VLM with the ability to reason about video content and use external tools to identify subtle inconsistencies, mirroring human system 2 thinking. 我们的方法使VLM能够对视频内容进行推理，并使用外部工具来识别微妙的不一致性，从而反映人类系统2的思维。\nOur self-evolving VLM dynamically selects and composes appropriate tools, enhancing its ability to generalize to novel video generation techniques. 我们的自我进化VLM动态选择和组合适当的工具，增强其推广到新颖视频生成技术的能力。\nThe modular design promotes interpretability, allowing for a clearer understanding of VLM's decision-making process. 模块化设计提高了可解释性，从而更清楚地了解VLM的决策过程。\nTo evaluate, we establish the first benchmark VidForensic containing 1.4k+ high-quality AI-generated videos across eight generative models. 为了进行评估，我们在八个生成模型中建立了第一个包含1.4k+高质量AI生成视频的基准VidForensic。\nExperiments show that REVEAL improves F1 scores by 9.1% to 30.2% over top baselines across our datasets for VLMs, notably for GPT-4o, Gemini 1.5 pro, and QWen-VL-Max, and Llava-One-Vision-7B. 实验表明，在我们的VLM数据集中， REVEL将F1分数比最高基线提高了9.1%至30.2% ，尤其是GPT-4o、Gemini 1.5 pro和QWen-VL-Max以及Llava-One-Vision-7B。\nWhile open-world AI-video detection remains an open challenge, our results indicate that existing methods fail primarily because they lack tool-enabled, higher-order reasoning. 虽然开放世界的人工智能视频检测仍然是一个公开的挑战，但我们的结果表明，现有方法之所以失败，主要是因为它们缺乏工具支持的高阶推理。",
