          "summary": "AI agents are rapidly improving in cybersecurity when source code is available, yet much of the software most consequential to security, including malware, firmware, and proprietary applications, exists only as binaries. 当源代码可用时，人工智能代理在网络安全方面正在迅速改进，但大多数与安全最相关的软件，包括恶意软件、固件和专有应用程序，仅作为二进制文件存在。\nAnalyzing such software requires reverse engineering (RE): recovering program semantics before analysis can proceed. 分析此类软件需要逆向工程（ RE ） ：在进行分析之前恢复程序语义。\nEvaluating agentic RE poses a fundamental challenge: realistic benchmark instances must (1) be absent from LLMs' training data to prevent shortcuts by memorization, and (2) reflect the scale and anti-analysis protections of real-world binaries. 评估代理RE提出了一个根本性的挑战：现实的基准实例必须（ 1 ）在LLM的训练数据中缺失，以防止记忆的快捷方式，以及（ 2 ）反映现实世界二进制的规模和反分析保护。\nWe introduce SRE-Bench, the first realistic, contamination-free RE benchmark. 我们引入了SRE-Bench ，这是第一个实际的无污染可再生能源基准。\nBuilt from scratch by RE experts with over 5,000 expert hours, SRE-Bench comprises 19 private, real-world-scale programs averaging 16.9K lines of code. SRE-Bench由可再生能源专家从零开始构建，拥有超过5,000个专家小时，由19个私有、真实世界规模的程序组成，平均每个程序有16.9K行代码。\nWe further developed 44 in-house anti-analysis mechanisms, yielding 262 binary instances and 1,572 deterministically graded tasks. 我们进一步开发了44种内部反分析机制，产生了262个二进制实例和1,572个确定性分级任务。\nWe evaluated 13 agentic settings across 11 models: eight in public-facing settings and five in internal unconstrained settings with cyber safeguards disabled and no budget cap. 我们评估了11个模型中的13个代理设置： 8个在面向公众的设置中， 5个在禁用网络安全措施且没有预算上限的内部无限制设置中。\nRealistic RE remains challenging for frontier agents: GPT-5.6-Sol and Claude-Fable-5.1, despite strong source-code security capabilities, fully solve only 31.5% and 26.9% of graded instances, suggesting that success in source-code security does not translate into effective binary analysis. 对于前沿代理商来说，现实的RE仍然具有挑战性： GPT-5.6-Sol和Claude-Fable-5.1 ，尽管具有强大的源代码安全能力，但仅完全解决了31.5%和26.9%的分级实例，这表明源代码安全的成功并不能转化为有效的二进制分析。\nWithout a budget cap and safety guard, GPT-6-Astra achieves a near-perfect pass@4 score, yet reliably identifying the correct candidate remains difficult. 在没有预算上限和安全防护的情况下， GPT-6-Astra在4分时获得了近乎完美的通过，但仍然很难可靠地确定正确的候选人。\nAgents are largely insensitive to compiler optimization and static linking, and ablations confirm that both contamination control and realistic scale are essential to understanding agents' RE capability. 代理在很大程度上对编译器优化和静态链接不敏感，消融证实了污染控制和现实规模对于理解代理的可再生能源能力至关重要。\nThese findings highlight RE as a distinct frontier for agentic cybersecurity and establish SRE-Bench as a rigorous testbed for measuring progress. 这些发现强调RE是代理网络安全的独特前沿，并将SRE-Bench确立为衡量进展的严格测试平台。",
