          "summary": "As LLM agents are increasingly deployed in multi-agent systems, they introduce risks of covert coordination that may evade standard forms of human oversight. 随着LLM代理越来越多地部署在多代理系统中，它们引入了可能逃避标准形式的人类监督的秘密协调风险。\nWhile linear probes on model activations have shown promise for detecting deception in single-agent settings, collusion is inherently a multi-agent phenomenon, and the use of internal representations for detecting collusion between agents remains unexplored. 虽然模型激活的线性探针已显示出在单代理设置中检测欺骗的前景，但勾结本质上是一种多代理现象，并且使用内部表示来检测代理之间的勾结仍未得到探索。\nWe introduce NARCBench, a benchmark for evaluating collusion detection under environment distribution shift, and propose five probing techniques that aggregate per-agent deception scores to classify scenarios at the group level, evaluated across four open-weight models (Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.1-70B, DeepSeek-R1 32B, GPT-OSS-20B) and six probe architectures. 我们引入了NARCBench ，这是评估环境分布变化下的勾结检测的基准，并提出了五种探测技术，汇总每个代理的欺骗分数，以便在组级别对场景进行分类，这些技术在四个开放权重模型（ Qwen3-32B ， Llama-3.1-70B ， DeepSeek-R1 32B ， GPT-OSS-20B ）和六个探测架构中进行了评估。\nWe frame this as a distributed anomaly detection problem, identifying three collusion signatures that map onto distinct anomaly types and detection paradigms. 我们将其视为分布式异常检测问题，识别映射到不同异常类型和检测范式的三个勾结特征。\nEvery model reaches 1.00 AUROC in-distribution; on our strongest model (Llama-3.1-70B), our five probing techniques achieve 0.73 to 0.93 AUROC when transferred zero-shot to structurally different multi-agent scenarios and 0.99 to 1.00 on a steganographic blackjack card-counting task, with detection performance scaling with model capability. 每个模型都达到1.00 AUROC分布；在我们最强的模型（ Llama-3.1-70B ）上，我们的五种探测技术在将零点转移到结构不同的多代理场景时实现0.73至0.93 AUROC ，在隐写二十一点卡片计数任务中实现0.99至1.00 ，并具有模型功能的检测性能缩放。\nWe find that no single probing technique dominates across all collusion types, consistent with the framework's prediction that different anomaly types require different detection paradigms. 我们发现，没有单一的探测技术在所有勾结类型中占主导地位，这与框架的预测一致，即不同的异常类型需要不同的检测范式。\nThis work takes a step toward multi-agent interpretability: extending white-box inspection from single models to multi-agent contexts, where detection requires aggregating signals across agents. 这项工作朝着多Agent可解释性迈出了一步：将白盒检查从单个模型扩展到多Agent上下文，其中检测需要跨Agent聚合信号。\nThese results suggest that model internals provide a complementary signal to text-level monitoring for detecting multi-agent collusion. 这些结果表明，模型内部为文本级监控提供了补充信号，用于检测多智能体勾结。\nCode and data available at https://github.com/aaronrose227/narcbench. 代码和数据可在https://github.com/aaronrose227/narcbench上获得。",
